1
00:00:06,428 --> 00:02:04,098
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries

2
00:02:04,098 --> 00:02:08,478
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:03:00,495 --> 00:03:03,315
Karayel! Come on!

4
00:03:58,803 --> 00:04:02,193
Osman got down from the horse.
The horse went this way.

5
00:04:09,236 --> 00:04:10,806
Useless!

6
00:04:12,218 --> 00:04:13,638
What kind of a scout are you?

7
00:04:18,687 --> 00:04:20,667
I can't bear foolishness.

8
00:04:30,621 --> 00:04:32,681
He wants us to scatter.

9
00:04:36,135 --> 00:04:40,135
If we can't find Osman,
Balgay will kill us all!

10
00:04:41,122 --> 00:04:42,372
Let's go!

11
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:49,061
Kongar!

12
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:53,240
Its time for you to either
return to your roots...

13
00:04:54,296 --> 00:04:55,476
... or...

14
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,320
... its time for you to die.

15
00:05:42,807 --> 00:05:45,387
Running away! He's running away!

16
00:05:47,047 --> 00:05:48,837
He's running away!

17
00:05:57,900 --> 00:05:59,610
He's running away, my Gündüz!

18
00:06:00,393 --> 00:06:02,493
We can't catch up without horses,
Bamsı Bey.

19
00:06:02,493 --> 00:06:05,923
You red rat!

20
00:06:06,563 --> 00:06:11,483
Son! Sofia is definitely involved in this.

21
00:06:11,552 --> 00:06:15,552
Since Saltuk also came, someone from
the Tent is also involved, Bamsı Bey.

22
00:06:16,138 --> 00:06:19,828
Then all the signs lead to Dündar.

23
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:26,470
What if Dündar is working with Alişar?

24
00:06:28,512 --> 00:06:31,652
My uncle was with us.
He wouldn't have done it.

25
00:06:33,842 --> 00:06:39,062
Son. What if he came to us
so someone else could do it?

26
00:06:39,464 --> 00:06:42,584
What if all the autocracy was for this?

27
00:06:43,543 --> 00:06:47,123
My Gündüz! He has a lot of
men in the Tent too!

28
00:06:48,903 --> 00:06:52,643
Son! Don't give yourself up
to your emotions.

29
00:06:53,576 --> 00:06:55,726
Don't you do it, son.

30
00:06:57,715 --> 00:07:00,945
We'll figure this out, Bamsı Bey.
We'll figure it out.

31
00:07:01,783 --> 00:07:05,783
Let's just pray that Zorba stays alive.

32
00:07:06,831 --> 00:07:08,631
Let's go.

33
00:07:35,935 --> 00:07:40,575
Kongar is still after me. You must
convince him before its too late.

34
00:07:42,033 --> 00:07:44,853
I have completed your order.

35
00:07:45,392 --> 00:07:50,192
Here is the proof that Balgay bought
Kongar, my brother Göktuğ...

36
00:07:50,192 --> 00:07:51,862
... from the slave market.

37
00:08:13,773 --> 00:08:18,233
Your brother Göktuğ will also
see Balgay's real face.

38
00:08:19,058 --> 00:08:21,408
What was hidden is now evident.

39
00:08:22,896 --> 00:08:25,676
Even though he is my brother
Göktuğ either believes us ...

40
00:08:25,676 --> 00:08:27,716
... or faces the consequences.

41
00:08:31,955 --> 00:08:34,965
Instead of a traitor brother...

42
00:08:36,949 --> 00:08:39,799
... I'd rather have a dead brother.

43
00:08:43,988 --> 00:08:47,578
Praise be! Karayel!

44
00:09:00,175 --> 00:09:01,765
My heart, my soul.

45
00:09:38,865 --> 00:09:42,255
So, you went to get herbs with
the cart, Zöhre Hatun.

46
00:09:42,255 --> 00:09:44,545
Right before your daughter
was going to marry.

47
00:09:46,209 --> 00:09:48,799
If something happens to Osman's legacy...

48
00:09:49,598 --> 00:09:52,358
... I will show mercy to none of you.

49
00:10:34,991 --> 00:10:38,991
My lovely daughters!
Demirci Bey's valiant Alps!

50
00:10:39,214 --> 00:10:42,234
The sledge is here. Prepare it.

51
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:51,490
You're on your own from now on.

52
00:11:09,407 --> 00:11:11,747
The person you're going to
deliver the girl to...

53
00:11:11,747 --> 00:11:14,137
... will be waiting for you
by the Cehennem Creek.

54
00:11:14,137 --> 00:11:16,527
Let's go. We don't have much time.

55
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:24,300
- Hope no one saw a thing.
- No, Zöhre Hatun. No.

56
00:11:25,128 --> 00:11:28,398
What is it, Burçin?
You're shaking like a leaf.

57
00:11:29,049 --> 00:11:32,009
I say no one saw us.
But what if someone did?

58
00:11:32,629 --> 00:11:34,849
What if people find out?

59
00:11:35,087 --> 00:11:38,237
If we were afraid of people finding out...

60
00:11:38,712 --> 00:11:41,412
... we wouldn't have moved an inch.

61
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:48,516
People will eventually find out.
Don't you get it?

62
00:11:48,673 --> 00:11:53,083
You have completed the duty
our Martyr son Aybars left unfinished.

63
00:11:53,543 --> 00:11:59,103
We do what we do for the future
of Kayı and the future of our children.

64
00:11:59,439 --> 00:12:02,589
Otherwise, why would we have
anything to do with this poor lady?

65
00:12:02,589 --> 00:12:07,089
What we want is Dündar Bey
to get back the throne he deserves...

66
00:12:07,375 --> 00:12:09,775
... and bring order once again.

67
00:12:09,775 --> 00:12:15,795
If we have to give up our lives for
this cause, we will!

68
00:12:17,312 --> 00:12:20,522
Relax. You did the right thing.

69
00:12:20,932 --> 00:12:22,752
I got your back.

70
00:12:36,777 --> 00:12:37,927
Let's go.

71
00:12:45,635 --> 00:12:51,355
We went to get gather herbs. The cart is
loaded. If someone asks, we aren't lying.

72
00:12:51,355 --> 00:12:55,035
Now it's obvious that you're
Dündar Bey's daughter, my Aygül.

73
00:12:55,146 --> 00:12:59,456
- My smart daughter. Do you have the bell?
- I do, mother.

74
00:13:13,158 --> 00:13:14,378
They...

75
00:13:16,353 --> 00:13:19,173
... will be waiting for you
at the rocky side of the creek.

76
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:21,193
Ring this bell when you get close.

77
00:13:21,712 --> 00:13:25,682
After you hear the response,
you'll find them. Go.

78
00:13:26,077 --> 00:13:28,287
Good luck. May Allah protect you.

79
00:13:57,275 --> 00:13:59,235
Now tell me!

80
00:14:01,166 --> 00:14:03,806
Who killed Batur?

81
00:14:04,436 --> 00:14:06,616
- Batur--
- Yes?

82
00:14:09,339 --> 00:14:12,399
The one who killed Batur--

83
00:14:36,839 --> 00:14:40,509
He didn't live long enough.
He died, poor thing.

84
00:14:57,382 --> 00:15:02,472
My Gündüz! One died. Let's keep
the other one alive. Relax, son.

85
00:15:07,701 --> 00:15:09,241
Bamsı Bey!

86
00:15:10,434 --> 00:15:14,434
We'll take this Saltuk
to my uncle's side.

87
00:15:15,325 --> 00:15:20,985
We'll see if he knew about
the betrayal or not.

88
00:15:21,285 --> 00:15:26,625
We will, son. We will. Just relax.
Relax, my Gündüz.

89
00:15:34,911 --> 00:15:39,501
Geyhatu is playing a wicked game.

90
00:15:41,765 --> 00:15:46,385
He is in an alliance with a dark
league inside Byzantium.

91
00:15:52,092 --> 00:15:56,482
This organization's name is
Monks of Margaret.

92
00:15:58,028 --> 00:16:02,028
They are the ones who sent
Yannis and Sofia after us.

93
00:16:03,143 --> 00:16:06,613
Through this organization,
Geyhatu wants to...

94
00:16:06,613 --> 00:16:11,163
... put someone he's collaborating with
to the throne of Byzantine.

95
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,700
The only thing we can do
to find this person...

96
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:20,540
... and prevent a possible
Turk massacre in these lands...

97
00:16:21,771 --> 00:16:24,421
... is to attack them
when they get together.

98
00:16:25,572 --> 00:16:29,572
What is your order, my Bey?
We can cut them all.

99
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:33,328
No doubt, Konur brother.
But...

100
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:36,575
You won't come.

101
00:16:37,461 --> 00:16:39,271
I will go.

102
00:16:40,309 --> 00:16:43,989
My Bey, we can't leave you alone
in such a dangerous duty.

103
00:16:43,989 --> 00:16:46,199
That's the order, Boran brother.

104
00:16:47,732 --> 00:16:49,452
You won't come, I said.

105
00:16:53,249 --> 00:16:55,569
You will go to the Tent, to my brother.

106
00:16:56,804 --> 00:17:00,804
And you will take care of Kongar.

107
00:17:03,858 --> 00:17:05,338
Besides...

108
00:17:06,158 --> 00:17:08,088
Who said I was alone?

109
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:12,790
In this important duty...

110
00:17:13,656 --> 00:17:15,906
... I too have a companion.

111
00:17:22,677 --> 00:17:24,467
Tell us, my Bey.

112
00:17:24,962 --> 00:17:27,552
Who is this valiant
that will accompany you?

113
00:17:27,552 --> 00:17:31,552
A warrior who dedicates
his life to his traditions.

114
00:17:32,392 --> 00:17:37,392
Someone great enough
to seep into these Monks.

115
00:17:42,823 --> 00:17:45,683
Everything in this world has a purpose.

116
00:17:46,185 --> 00:17:49,805
Lightning strikes, thunder cracks.

117
00:17:50,048 --> 00:17:54,048
Water runs, Turkish
mothers give birth to valiants.

118
00:17:54,163 --> 00:17:56,873
Thank you, Konur brother.

119
00:18:01,755 --> 00:18:04,715
But Geyhatu is aware of this valiant.

120
00:18:05,133 --> 00:18:10,753
I worry that both his life
and his trick is in danger.

121
00:18:11,921 --> 00:18:16,731
My duty is to stop Commander Böke,
who was sent by Geyhatu.

122
00:18:17,539 --> 00:18:22,459
Böke is coming to reveal this valiant
who seeped into the Monks.

123
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:26,053
They are in the Dark Alley near
the Mount Monk.

124
00:18:26,053 --> 00:18:27,743
They will meet here.

125
00:18:34,601 --> 00:18:37,831
Mount Monk...
There it is, my Bey.

126
00:18:43,095 --> 00:18:47,445
But be careful.
It's not our territory.

127
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:51,844
Don't you worry, Konur brother.

128
00:18:51,982 --> 00:18:57,292
Our valiants are wolves!
And the lands we step on are our homes!

129
00:19:00,889 --> 00:19:04,889
You will see.
The day will come...

130
00:19:05,805 --> 00:19:10,855
... and the crescent will shine
upon these lands.

131
00:19:16,961 --> 00:19:21,211
Allah willing, my Bey.
Allah willing.

132
00:19:42,776 --> 00:19:46,776
We'll rest here.
We won't stop until the meeting.

133
00:20:07,534 --> 00:20:10,534
Get up on the hill.
See if anyone is following us.

134
00:20:30,216 --> 00:20:32,826
You look a little worried, Master Hiristo.

135
00:20:57,009 --> 00:21:01,509
I'm full of joy since we
will be getting rid of the Turks.

136
00:21:02,586 --> 00:21:06,586
But I'm afraid of the consequences
of working with Mongols.

137
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:14,242
And also of the new Emperor
after we get the current one down.

138
00:21:16,219 --> 00:21:20,039
Is he going to be powerful enough
to treat the Turks the way they deserve?

139
00:21:20,591 --> 00:21:23,841
- Are we sure?
- I know that he is ambitious.

140
00:21:24,125 --> 00:21:26,235
He grew up with hatred towards Turks.

141
00:21:26,423 --> 00:21:30,223
Merciless. Smart.

142
00:21:33,084 --> 00:21:38,644
Who is he? Who is this person who is
kept hidden from me and all the Monks?

143
00:21:45,525 --> 00:21:50,765
You will find out when we get together
with the other Monks, Master Hiristo.

144
00:23:12,330 --> 00:23:13,940
Are we sure?

145
00:23:30,667 --> 00:23:33,967
So you are the snake who poisoned us!

146
00:23:36,313 --> 00:23:38,963
We won't let you work with the Mongols!

147
00:23:41,055 --> 00:23:42,245
Kill him!

148
00:24:22,170 --> 00:24:24,190
Burn in hell, Turk!

149
00:24:34,057 --> 00:24:36,387
We'll be your hell.

150
00:25:19,331 --> 00:25:20,621
Traitor!

151
00:26:44,881 --> 00:26:48,881
We brought the baggage safe and sound.
It's your business now.

152
00:26:49,364 --> 00:26:55,624
Dündar Bey did a good job.
Alişar Bey sends his regards.

153
00:26:56,813 --> 00:26:59,363
- Goodbye.
- Thank you.

154
00:27:08,197 --> 00:27:11,787
You'll do a lot of our work for us.

155
00:27:16,392 --> 00:27:22,392
She's all exposed. Soldiers!
Put something over her.

156
00:27:22,392 --> 00:27:24,312
Let's get out of here.

157
00:27:27,159 --> 00:27:29,109
She'll catch up.

158
00:27:38,722 --> 00:27:40,872
Isn't that Saltuk?

159
00:27:44,915 --> 00:27:46,935
What did he do?

160
00:28:05,998 --> 00:28:07,998
Put him in the caged tent.

161
00:28:10,285 --> 00:28:11,735
Dündar...

162
00:28:16,261 --> 00:28:22,121
Let's go ask uncle Marife, Bamsı Bey.
He could read Zorba's eyes.

163
00:28:23,033 --> 00:28:28,843
Dündar...
Is it you behind this too?

164
00:28:51,161 --> 00:28:54,961
What is it, Boran? Why are you alone?
Where is Osman?

165
00:28:54,961 --> 00:28:56,781
My Bey is on duty.

166
00:28:58,428 --> 00:29:01,318
He sent me here. Maybe I could help.

167
00:29:01,595 --> 00:29:05,595
What duty is this, Boran?
What if he gets in trouble?

168
00:29:05,797 --> 00:29:09,567
He told me to go, Bamsı Bey.
He'll tell you the rest himself.

169
00:29:09,835 --> 00:29:12,195
My Bey's orders. I can't tell you.

170
00:29:15,030 --> 00:29:16,950
Let's go, Bamsı Bey.

171
00:29:19,950 --> 00:29:22,660
Gündüz! Bamsı Bey! Wait!

172
00:29:26,383 --> 00:29:28,783
What is it, aunt? What happened?

173
00:29:30,695 --> 00:29:33,785
My Gündüz. Princess Adelfa isn't here.

174
00:29:35,893 --> 00:29:38,453
Bala went to look for her.

175
00:29:40,444 --> 00:29:46,054
Boran! Get the Alps and look for her. Go!
Go, my valiant!

176
00:29:46,334 --> 00:29:49,734
- Okay, my Bey!
- Go, quick!

177
00:29:50,469 --> 00:29:53,399
My uncle is on dangerous waters, my Bey.

178
00:29:54,220 --> 00:30:00,600
As we ignore everything he does,
he is getting more mad by the day.

179
00:30:01,308 --> 00:30:04,388
You stay, aunt.
We'll go and talk to him.

180
00:30:04,388 --> 00:30:11,668
You can't find him, my Gündüz. Dündar
Bey, Zöhre and Aygül are not in the Tent.

181
00:30:13,918 --> 00:30:20,668
I don't know what they're up to.
But they have disappeared.

182
00:30:20,668 --> 00:30:28,558
This Dündar is asking for it!
I don't like where this is going.

183
00:30:29,959 --> 00:30:33,959
He'll return here eventually.
We should remain calm.

184
00:30:34,896 --> 00:30:36,996
We'll stand up to him when he is here.

185
00:30:36,996 --> 00:30:40,486
Let's see what he'll do
when we tell him that we have Saltuk.

186
00:30:45,135 --> 00:30:50,505
For my father's sake, I say.
He is my uncle, I say.

187
00:30:51,244 --> 00:30:53,724
But he still does his thing.

188
00:30:55,744 --> 00:30:56,764
Pity.

189
00:30:58,916 --> 00:30:59,796
Pity.

190
00:31:05,270 --> 00:31:08,870
- I shot Zorba as you ordered, father.
- Is he dead?

191
00:31:08,870 --> 00:31:10,470
He's dead, father.

192
00:31:10,675 --> 00:31:12,525
My mad lion!

193
00:31:13,680 --> 00:31:15,740
Your father would die for you!

194
00:31:16,060 --> 00:31:18,390
Did anyone saw or got suspicious?

195
00:31:18,390 --> 00:31:22,480
No one saw me. But they caught Saltuk.

196
00:31:24,472 --> 00:31:28,112
- That's not good.
- Saltuk's mouth is sealed shut, father.

197
00:31:28,570 --> 00:31:32,490
No knife known to man can make him talk.

198
00:31:32,726 --> 00:31:35,406
Hopefully, son. Hopefully.

199
00:31:35,834 --> 00:31:39,834
I don't care if he tells
everything he knows.

200
00:31:39,990 --> 00:31:45,590
Now that you're here, my back is
more straight, my hands are more powerful!

201
00:31:46,606 --> 00:31:52,866
- Thank you, father.
- How is your mother Hazal Hatun doing?

202
00:31:53,644 --> 00:31:57,394
Didn't she want to come? Did she
forget the routes?

203
00:31:57,768 --> 00:32:00,908
She's a Bey's daughter, you know.
Obeys the traditions.

204
00:32:01,436 --> 00:32:04,356
She won't move until you order
her to come.

205
00:32:04,672 --> 00:32:07,482
But only I know the longing in her eyes.

206
00:32:07,652 --> 00:32:16,802
She'll come, son. She will.
After we clean our path, she will come.

207
00:32:16,802 --> 00:32:21,252
You're bad with each other because of me.
I've made a big mistake.

208
00:32:23,331 --> 00:32:25,561
Are you still mad at me, father?

209
00:32:25,561 --> 00:32:29,521
Big Tents have big problems, son.

210
00:32:29,856 --> 00:32:33,426
You were right in your own way.
And so was I.

211
00:32:33,695 --> 00:32:40,525
So was your mother who
said, "If my son is exiled, so am I."

212
00:32:48,711 --> 00:32:51,291
My Bey. We've delivered Adelfa.

213
00:32:58,286 --> 00:33:01,636
People of the Tent think that we're
still bad with each other.

214
00:33:01,636 --> 00:33:06,416
Let it remain that way.
So we can play our game with ease.

215
00:33:06,620 --> 00:33:12,030
Go to the Tent.
Use this hostility as a weapon.

216
00:33:12,851 --> 00:33:16,851
Let them think that we
still hate each other.

217
00:33:16,990 --> 00:33:20,310
So that they give something away.

218
00:33:21,741 --> 00:33:25,331
I'll pay a visit to Alişar Bey.

219
00:33:26,051 --> 00:33:27,941
As you order, father.

220
00:34:55,417 --> 00:34:58,907
The spirit of Margaret took root.

221
00:34:58,907 --> 00:35:01,577
- Forever!
- Forever.

222
00:35:04,317 --> 00:35:06,067
Brother! What happened?

223
00:35:11,249 --> 00:35:14,879
Master Dennis.
They killed master Dennis.

224
00:35:15,574 --> 00:35:18,854
May God protect us!
Who did this to you, brother?

225
00:35:18,854 --> 00:35:20,514
The Turks!

226
00:35:20,514 --> 00:35:23,784
Hurry up! Let's take him to Master Tilsus.

227
00:35:41,246 --> 00:35:44,186
This is the truth, I say to you.

228
00:35:45,002 --> 00:35:52,492
It doesn't have life in it before it eats
humans' flesh and drinks humans' blood.

229
00:35:52,492 --> 00:35:59,452
Those who eat my flesh and drink
my blood have eternal lives.

230
00:35:59,672 --> 00:36:03,672
And I will bless them in my final days.

231
00:36:03,938 --> 00:36:12,038
Because my flesh is genuine food,
my blood is a genuine drink.

232
00:36:55,892 --> 00:36:59,892
Master Hiristo!
Where is Master Dennis?

233
00:37:00,566 --> 00:37:04,566
- We were attacked, Tesius.
- Who did this?

234
00:37:05,450 --> 00:37:06,720
The Turks!

235
00:37:07,583 --> 00:37:11,173
- How many were they?
- There were more than 20 Turk warriors.

236
00:37:11,629 --> 00:37:14,219
- Most of them died.
- Do they know where we are?

237
00:37:14,219 --> 00:37:18,389
- No.
- How can you be so sure, Master Hiristo?

238
00:37:18,917 --> 00:37:22,347
They tortured Master Dennis
to find out our meeting spot.

239
00:37:23,857 --> 00:37:28,287
I found a way and killed him
so that he didn't suffer.

240
00:37:31,662 --> 00:37:35,242
May Mother Mary forgive me.
May she forgive my sins.

241
00:37:35,242 --> 00:37:38,902
Master Dennis was both
a mother and a father to me.

242
00:37:41,592 --> 00:37:44,842
Master Tesius.
Believe me, you're safe here.

243
00:37:45,576 --> 00:37:48,126
You did something great, Master Hiristo.

244
00:37:49,676 --> 00:37:53,676
But we should still be careful.
Everyone to their positions!

245
00:37:53,676 --> 00:37:58,656
Take your precautions. If there were no
traitors among us...

246
00:37:58,656 --> 00:38:02,096
... it would be impossible for them
to know our meeting spot. Quick!

247
00:38:02,580 --> 00:38:03,980
Quick, I said!

248
00:42:16,275 --> 00:42:21,215
My mouth is bubbling from hunger.
Light a fire.

249
00:42:21,709 --> 00:42:23,669
I will hunt.

250
00:43:33,546 --> 00:43:35,396
Osman!

251
00:43:36,585 --> 00:43:39,125
I'll find you eventually, Osman!

252
00:43:39,153 --> 00:43:41,213
You can't find him unless he wants you to.

253
00:43:50,705 --> 00:43:52,085
Where is Osman?

254
00:43:52,854 --> 00:43:54,544
What are you doing here?

255
00:43:54,544 --> 00:43:59,114
He's loyal to his alliance with Balgay.
Firstly, remember that.

256
00:44:01,748 --> 00:44:03,378
And about me...

257
00:44:05,039 --> 00:44:07,049
I'm looking for you.

258
00:44:08,225 --> 00:44:13,105
Do you want to fight alone? Is that why
you walk so sneakily?

259
00:44:13,105 --> 00:44:17,465
If I wanted to fight, we would
have done it by now.

260
00:44:19,693 --> 00:44:22,093
I don't want to fight you.

261
00:44:22,947 --> 00:44:26,067
I want you to learn the truth and
return to your roots.

262
00:44:26,154 --> 00:44:30,494
I protect my roots.
I fight on a horse like a brave Mongol!

263
00:44:33,961 --> 00:44:37,181
You even don't believe what you've said.

264
00:44:39,934 --> 00:44:41,864
You think you are a Mongol.

265
00:44:42,582 --> 00:44:44,512
You also believe the tales you
memorize.

266
00:44:45,170 --> 00:44:46,860
You think I am still your brother.

267
00:44:48,015 --> 00:44:49,095
Tales, huh?

268
00:44:52,537 --> 00:44:53,697
Look at this.

269
00:44:57,628 --> 00:44:58,838
Is it a tale as well?

270
00:45:02,890 --> 00:45:03,920
What's this?

271
00:45:04,057 --> 00:45:07,677
A document that shows you being bought
from a slave market by Balgay.

272
00:45:10,298 --> 00:45:12,058
He hides the truth from you.

273
00:45:14,038 --> 00:45:14,778
Take it!

274
00:45:15,283 --> 00:45:16,913
See it with your own eyes.

275
00:46:04,957 --> 00:46:05,727
Göktuğ.

276
00:46:06,267 --> 00:46:07,017
Göktuğ.

277
00:46:07,047 --> 00:46:08,317
Come here, my son.

278
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:22,290
Oh! I have the same thing on me.

279
00:46:23,031 --> 00:46:24,411
Of course you have, son.

280
00:46:24,483 --> 00:46:27,243
We have it on all of our soldiers.

281
00:46:27,745 --> 00:46:28,455
Argh.

282
00:46:51,823 --> 00:46:52,583
Father.

283
00:46:52,753 --> 00:46:53,473
Father.

284
00:46:53,894 --> 00:46:54,594
Konur.

285
00:46:55,015 --> 00:46:55,805
Göktuğ.

286
00:46:58,768 --> 00:46:59,518
Father!

287
00:47:01,163 --> 00:47:02,253
- Father!
- Wake up.

288
00:47:02,356 --> 00:47:03,186
Father!

289
00:47:15,582 --> 00:47:16,502
Father!

290
00:47:22,076 --> 00:47:25,786
These tyrants use our
brave men against us.

291
00:47:28,807 --> 00:47:30,257
Pull yourself together.

292
00:47:31,225 --> 00:47:32,755
Be yourself, Göktuğ.

293
00:47:37,639 --> 00:47:40,749
Don't forget that everything
turns back to its roots.

294
00:47:41,505 --> 00:47:45,505
Wolves to wolves.
Dogs to dogs.

295
00:48:40,320 --> 00:48:41,830
The mad one is coming.

296
00:48:42,966 --> 00:48:44,346
Don't give something away.

297
00:48:44,606 --> 00:48:46,016
Leave this to me.

298
00:48:53,218 --> 00:48:54,378
May it be easy.

299
00:48:56,775 --> 00:48:58,805
If you think that's easy,
come and do it.

300
00:49:04,326 --> 00:49:05,476
What's that?

301
00:49:06,171 --> 00:49:09,931
Do you use cars to gather herbs now,
Zöhre?

302
00:49:12,241 --> 00:49:14,041
You see it with your own eyes.

303
00:49:14,231 --> 00:49:17,221
How could we carry all those things?

304
00:49:19,354 --> 00:49:22,414
When you meet with any obstacle, you
know looking for a cure.

305
00:49:23,325 --> 00:49:29,315
But you don't know how those ointments and
drugs are made.

306
00:49:30,844 --> 00:49:33,204
Meeting with an obstacle isn't
something bad.

307
00:49:33,531 --> 00:49:37,531
The soldiers of Tent are dying for the
prosperity of Tent.

308
00:49:37,877 --> 00:49:40,787
If you feel offended doing this, don't do.

309
00:49:40,863 --> 00:49:42,753
We'll do it with the help of Allah.

310
00:49:46,232 --> 00:49:47,192
Tell me.

311
00:49:47,958 --> 00:49:49,538
Did you see Bala Hatun?

312
00:49:52,442 --> 00:49:56,442
We didn't see or hear anything,
Selcan Hatun.

313
00:49:58,293 --> 00:50:00,673
You look like your mother over time.

314
00:50:00,868 --> 00:50:01,758
What a pity!

315
00:50:04,533 --> 00:50:06,943
Tell me, Zöhre.

316
00:50:07,403 --> 00:50:11,403
Bala Hatun and our guest have disappeared.

317
00:50:11,699 --> 00:50:14,199
If you know or hear anything, speak.

318
00:50:14,873 --> 00:50:18,783
If you don't speak even if you know,
I'll cut your tongue and you can't...

319
00:50:18,804 --> 00:50:20,344
...speak from that time.

320
00:50:28,911 --> 00:50:30,021
Look me, Hatun.

321
00:50:32,335 --> 00:50:36,815
When my daughter needs to get downry
ready, she is cleaning the herbs.

322
00:50:38,827 --> 00:50:44,027
When we need to do preparation for
wedding, we're working in here.

323
00:50:44,612 --> 00:50:46,182
What're you saying?

324
00:50:46,816 --> 00:50:48,436
It's a pity of you!

325
00:50:55,119 --> 00:50:58,189
Dündar Bey is not around for a long time.

326
00:50:58,380 --> 00:50:59,650
Where is he?

327
00:51:00,550 --> 00:51:02,910
Dündar Bey is in the grave of his son.

328
00:51:04,025 --> 00:51:06,575
Does he need to get permission from you?

329
00:51:07,018 --> 00:51:09,328
Those who are innocent can do whatever
they like.

330
00:51:09,328 --> 00:51:10,840
We can't say anything.

331
00:51:10,840 --> 00:51:13,420
But there is the shadow
of betrayal on you.

332
00:51:13,521 --> 00:51:14,691
We'll surely follow.

333
00:51:14,710 --> 00:51:15,900
We'll surely ask.

334
00:51:16,518 --> 00:51:20,858
If you are that curious, have
him followed.

335
00:51:22,436 --> 00:51:24,786
You are making me angry.

336
00:51:24,983 --> 00:51:27,493
We're doing our business.

337
00:51:28,046 --> 00:51:30,096
That's enough.

338
00:51:30,376 --> 00:51:31,386
Enough!

339
00:51:33,050 --> 00:51:36,420
Does it fit the dignity of ladies of
Kayıboyu to fight like this?

340
00:51:41,467 --> 00:51:42,487
Bahadır.

341
00:51:47,122 --> 00:51:48,552
Welcome, son.

342
00:51:59,419 --> 00:52:00,599
Zöhre Hatun.

343
00:52:00,797 --> 00:52:04,617
My mother, Selcan Hatun, tortured
Hazal Hatun.

344
00:52:05,585 --> 00:52:07,875
She never liked us.

345
00:52:09,867 --> 00:52:12,087
But Zöhre Hatun is married
with my Father.

346
00:52:12,601 --> 00:52:14,881
Don't treat her like that.

347
00:52:15,547 --> 00:52:16,947
This is not you.

348
00:52:17,752 --> 00:52:19,462
Where is Hazal Hatun, my son?

349
00:52:19,557 --> 00:52:20,817
Is she alright?

350
00:52:20,895 --> 00:52:22,015
She is alright.

351
00:52:22,665 --> 00:52:25,195
With the help of Allah, I hope she
will come here.

352
00:52:26,211 --> 00:52:29,851
We hope we will enjoy the
happiness of reuniting again.

353
00:52:30,303 --> 00:52:33,313
We hope that we will be together again.

354
00:52:45,855 --> 00:52:47,765
I hope we will be, brother.

355
00:52:49,942 --> 00:52:51,142
Welcome.

356
00:52:51,146 --> 00:52:52,806
How nice of you to come.

357
00:52:52,842 --> 00:52:56,992
Aygül, you are beautiful as moon,
my sister.

358
00:52:57,468 --> 00:52:58,498
Wonderful!

359
00:52:59,845 --> 00:53:02,765
Don't stay standing.
Let's go to the Tent.

360
00:53:02,976 --> 00:53:05,326
Tell me what you've done till now.

361
00:53:08,548 --> 00:53:10,638
You too come, Burçin Hatun.

362
00:53:24,568 --> 00:53:28,568
One period closes one period opens.

363
00:53:33,386 --> 00:53:36,536
There will be hard days for you, Zöhre.

364
00:53:37,080 --> 00:53:39,060
May Allah help you.

365
00:54:10,526 --> 00:54:11,736
Zorba died.

366
00:54:12,772 --> 00:54:19,632
I sent Bahadır to Tent so that he can
complete something left uncompleted.

367
00:54:20,155 --> 00:54:21,795
Did Bahadır come alone?

368
00:54:22,168 --> 00:54:24,388
He is with his sister and mother.

369
00:54:24,711 --> 00:54:26,651
In the Çobanoğulları land.

370
00:54:27,127 --> 00:54:29,077
He waits for my order.

371
00:54:29,660 --> 00:54:32,010
Çobanoğulları is a powerful seigniory.

372
00:54:32,155 --> 00:54:34,375
I didn't know that you were relatives.

373
00:54:35,740 --> 00:54:37,710
You're stronger from now on.

374
00:54:37,776 --> 00:54:41,196
Now we should wait for
the arrival of Osman.

375
00:54:41,782 --> 00:54:45,782
When he comes, we will create trouble
in Tent and get the the seigniory back.

376
00:54:47,619 --> 00:54:51,129
Wouldn't it be better not wait for
the arrival of him, Alisar Bey?

377
00:54:51,246 --> 00:54:52,036
It's not.

378
00:54:54,984 --> 00:54:57,104
We'll finish this job at once.

379
00:54:58,254 --> 00:55:01,224
We'll catch them in an unexpected time.

380
00:55:01,487 --> 00:55:03,177
Everyone is on the alert.

381
00:55:03,566 --> 00:55:06,276
When is the unexpected time?

382
00:55:09,593 --> 00:55:14,623
There's the fortitude of death and
relaxedness of marriage, Dündar Bey.

383
00:55:16,487 --> 00:55:22,547
No one will expect the beat at the
night of the marriage of me and Aygül.

384
00:56:09,697 --> 00:56:12,047
Welcome, Commander Böke.

385
00:56:19,075 --> 00:56:22,135
The big day has come, sir Tesius.

386
00:56:23,520 --> 00:56:25,160
Thanks to Geyhatu.

387
00:56:31,428 --> 00:56:34,138
Many cities will surrender without being
looted.

388
00:56:34,691 --> 00:56:38,011
The Constantinople will be in the
order of Geyhatu.

389
00:56:52,782 --> 00:56:58,582
If there hadn't been the Monks of Margaret,
too much blood would be spilt, Tesius.

390
00:57:02,468 --> 00:57:03,798
Let me introduce them.

391
00:57:04,208 --> 00:57:05,328
Monk Vanko.

392
00:57:07,417 --> 00:57:08,607
Monk Teron.

393
00:57:09,482 --> 00:57:10,672
Monk Hıristo.

394
00:57:17,162 --> 00:57:19,232
We've prepared a meal for you.

395
00:57:21,440 --> 00:57:22,440
Come on in.

396
00:57:37,267 --> 00:57:41,267
We've learned that Hıristo is a traitor.

397
00:58:46,159 --> 00:58:47,519
Look everywhere.

398
00:58:49,339 --> 00:58:50,669
You look this way.

399
00:58:50,777 --> 00:58:51,507
Hurry!

400
00:58:51,801 --> 00:58:52,501
Okay.

401
00:59:08,322 --> 00:59:10,152
Bala Hatun.

402
00:59:11,683 --> 00:59:14,683
How nice to see you again.

403
00:59:16,478 --> 00:59:17,978
Drop it!

404
00:59:18,064 --> 00:59:18,814
Now!

405
00:59:20,865 --> 00:59:21,635
Run!

406
00:59:38,359 --> 00:59:39,049
This way!

407
00:59:39,049 --> 00:59:39,859
Hurry!

408
00:59:40,666 --> 00:59:41,476
Soldiers!

409
00:59:43,766 --> 00:59:45,306
Hurry, fools!

410
00:59:51,283 --> 00:59:53,373
Someone took the Princess!

411
00:59:55,657 --> 00:59:57,067
We'll catch up to her later!

412
01:00:54,716 --> 01:01:00,816
A son of Kayı like you will be with you.

413
01:01:34,994 --> 01:01:36,714
How did you infiltrate?

414
01:01:38,867 --> 01:01:40,337
Who is behind you?

415
01:01:40,565 --> 01:01:41,715
Which power?

416
01:01:47,630 --> 01:01:49,030
Faith.

417
01:02:38,133 --> 01:02:39,323
It's no use.

418
01:02:40,223 --> 01:02:41,423
He'll not speak.

419
01:02:46,092 --> 01:02:47,212
Jesus save us.

420
01:02:49,315 --> 01:02:52,005
Turks know our all plan.

421
01:02:53,443 --> 01:02:57,773
We know every step and breath
you take, Tesius.

422
01:02:59,568 --> 01:03:01,798
You won't reach your goal.

423
01:04:10,048 --> 01:04:11,748
We need to go from here right now.

424
01:04:12,016 --> 01:04:14,456
Give me the names of spies in
the palace, Tesius.

425
01:04:17,536 --> 01:04:18,726
All here.

426
01:04:22,352 --> 01:04:26,352
But there are some issues
we need to agree on.

427
01:04:35,135 --> 01:04:37,345
We will agree certainly.

428
01:04:38,705 --> 01:04:42,705
You have your spies among
all people of the emperor.

429
01:04:42,870 --> 01:04:45,950
There's more than that, commander Böke.

430
01:04:46,436 --> 01:04:50,436
We need to dethrone the emperor before
our move is disclosed.

431
01:04:50,993 --> 01:04:52,543
Every minute counts.

432
01:04:52,853 --> 01:04:58,363
When the Princess Adelfa marries
Geyhatu, we will take gifts to the palace.

433
01:04:58,933 --> 01:05:04,773
Our soldiers who take gifts and your
spies will capture the palace with you.

434
01:05:06,898 --> 01:05:08,178
That's very good.

435
01:05:10,415 --> 01:05:11,565
What about him?

436
01:05:14,321 --> 01:05:15,441
He must die.

437
01:05:15,571 --> 01:05:17,921
His being alive is a big threat for us.

438
01:05:21,106 --> 01:05:22,636
I'll do this job.

439
01:06:28,219 --> 01:06:32,799
If that girl gets out alive from the
forest, you won't leave this forest alive.

440
01:06:33,053 --> 01:06:34,303
Did you understand?

441
01:06:34,681 --> 01:06:35,431
Come on!

442
01:06:35,905 --> 01:06:36,725
Come on!

443
01:07:10,263 --> 01:07:11,013
Kill her.

444
01:07:41,909 --> 01:07:42,679
I know.

445
01:07:44,697 --> 01:07:47,167
I made life miserable for you back
in the days.

446
01:07:48,328 --> 01:07:50,138
I must have hurt all of you.

447
01:07:52,735 --> 01:07:57,015
If it's like that, know that a different
Bahadır has come back.

448
01:07:58,852 --> 01:08:03,922
I want you to forget the
disappointments and old fights.

449
01:08:05,563 --> 01:08:10,463
We certainly don't want to hold grudge
and fall apart.

450
01:08:11,774 --> 01:08:15,574
You came.
Welcome.

451
01:08:16,465 --> 01:08:20,045
I hope your arrival
will be useful of our reuniting.

452
01:08:20,462 --> 01:08:21,732
Good luck with it.

453
01:08:21,893 --> 01:08:23,313
I hope so, Gündüz Bey.

454
01:08:23,322 --> 01:08:24,112
I hope so.

455
01:08:25,581 --> 01:08:29,641
But I don't know if my father will
accept me to his Tent.

456
01:08:31,852 --> 01:08:34,372
Firstly, I have to apologize.

457
01:08:35,988 --> 01:08:41,288
Then I want us to be strong and united
altogether.

458
01:08:44,101 --> 01:08:45,461
Of course we should be.

459
01:08:45,535 --> 01:08:49,135
When people of Kayı unite,
they can do whatever they want.

460
01:08:49,266 --> 01:08:51,016
They can wipe out enemies.

461
01:08:52,361 --> 01:08:53,881
I'm happy for your arrival.

462
01:08:53,947 --> 01:08:56,747
I'm happier for your
arrival with such kind words.

463
01:08:59,932 --> 01:09:03,302
If we talk about your father,
you will make it up certainly.

464
01:09:03,492 --> 01:09:04,362
It'll be okay.

465
01:09:09,268 --> 01:09:10,288
It'll be fine.

466
01:09:11,262 --> 01:09:12,632
It'll be okay certainly.

467
01:09:13,886 --> 01:09:15,696
My brother Batur has gone.

468
01:09:17,417 --> 01:09:21,077
But fortunately
our Allah didn't allow us to be alone.

469
01:09:26,542 --> 01:09:27,642
My Batur.

470
01:09:29,549 --> 01:09:31,799
You're irreplaceable, my son.

471
01:09:42,192 --> 01:09:43,512
You're right, Aygül.

472
01:09:45,421 --> 01:09:46,721
Another son...

473
01:09:47,169 --> 01:09:50,159
...from our blood...

474
01:09:51,657 --> 01:09:53,687
...only could relieve this pain.

475
01:10:00,405 --> 01:10:01,345
Bahadır.

476
01:10:02,293 --> 01:10:04,343
Let's get up if you like, my son.

477
01:10:04,778 --> 01:10:06,348
Thank you, Zöhre Hatun.

478
01:10:07,576 --> 01:10:09,436
Can I get your permission, Gündüz Bey?

479
01:10:10,280 --> 01:10:13,020
Yes.
You just rest.

480
01:10:13,809 --> 01:10:15,649
We can talk later.

481
01:10:15,660 --> 01:10:16,540
Thank you.

482
01:10:17,111 --> 01:10:19,941
But first,
I've some things to deal with.

483
01:10:21,532 --> 01:10:22,472
Selcan aunt.

484
01:10:23,474 --> 01:10:26,454
You' used to make very good bulghur rice.
I didn't forget that.

485
01:10:27,347 --> 01:10:30,767
If that's what you want,
I'll do it certainly.

486
01:10:30,802 --> 01:10:31,712
Thank you.

487
01:10:53,788 --> 01:10:55,488
My uncle isn't around still.

488
01:10:58,100 --> 01:11:02,100
I didn't want to cause disturbance
as Bahadır just has come.

489
01:11:02,183 --> 01:11:03,253
I didn't ask.

490
01:11:04,610 --> 01:11:06,220
But I'm not comfortable.

491
01:11:07,154 --> 01:11:09,734
Zöhre is trying to not give anything away.

492
01:11:09,936 --> 01:11:12,936
But a lie is not something secret.

493
01:11:13,426 --> 01:11:15,246
We'll disclose it.

494
01:11:16,643 --> 01:11:20,643
Did Dündar go to the grave of Batur
or not?

495
01:11:21,338 --> 01:11:22,708
Did you sort it out, son?

496
01:11:23,163 --> 01:11:26,213
Yes aunt, I sent an Alp.

497
01:11:26,373 --> 01:11:27,883
We'll see.

498
01:11:29,136 --> 01:11:30,096
We will, son.

499
01:11:30,809 --> 01:11:32,579
Then, we can smash them.

500
01:11:34,167 --> 01:11:38,167
We are tired of fighting with
the enemies inside us, anymore.

501
01:11:40,957 --> 01:11:42,587
That's enough.

502
01:11:49,373 --> 01:11:54,863
After you dethrone the emperor,
puppet emperor will use you Böke.

503
01:11:55,791 --> 01:11:59,101
Then, they'll get rid of you
as soon as possible.

504
01:11:59,877 --> 01:12:02,257
Not emperor.
Empress.

505
01:12:02,306 --> 01:12:03,716
You even don't know this.

506
01:12:03,834 --> 01:12:06,894
And you're trying to destroy
the friendship of us with Mongols.

507
01:12:06,938 --> 01:12:08,528
Look at your situation.

508
01:12:09,373 --> 01:12:12,513
An empress will save you, right?

509
01:12:13,503 --> 01:12:16,923
If you knew Sofia, you wouldn't
speak to me like that.

510
01:12:19,197 --> 01:12:20,227
Die Hıristo!

511
01:12:20,559 --> 01:12:21,489
Not Hıristo.

512
01:12:24,371 --> 01:12:26,521
The son of Süleyman Şah, Sungur.

513
01:12:35,483 --> 01:12:37,283
The uncle of Osman Bey?

514
01:12:37,974 --> 01:12:41,214
It seems you know Osman.

515
01:12:42,934 --> 01:12:44,944
You can kill me today, Böke.

516
01:12:45,711 --> 01:12:49,271
But our sprouting branches
will choke you.

517
01:12:51,110 --> 01:12:53,130
May witches take your life.

518
01:13:21,562 --> 01:13:23,312
Allah is eternal!

519
01:14:02,732 --> 01:14:03,782
Are you okay?

520
01:14:05,449 --> 01:14:06,179
Yes.

521
01:14:08,612 --> 01:14:10,662
Can you tell me your real name?

522
01:14:12,687 --> 01:14:15,437
The son of Süleyman Şah, Sungur Tekin.

523
01:14:20,831 --> 01:14:21,701
Uncle.

524
01:14:24,824 --> 01:14:25,754
Osman.

525
01:14:36,192 --> 01:14:36,982
Uncle.

526
01:14:41,573 --> 01:14:42,593
Wonderful!

527
01:14:50,572 --> 01:14:51,412
Uncle.

528
01:14:57,656 --> 01:14:58,686
Uncle.

529
01:15:08,269 --> 01:15:13,659
For years... We thought that you died in
Mongolian War, alongside uncle Gündoğdu.

530
01:15:14,833 --> 01:15:18,833
The flesh is mortal but the soul isn't.

531
01:15:24,246 --> 01:15:25,256
Uncle.

532
01:16:56,563 --> 01:16:59,203
May Allah bless your weapon with
sharpness, son.

533
01:17:07,593 --> 01:17:10,613
I wanted to speak to you before iftar.

534
01:17:11,273 --> 01:17:13,613
You saw me and lost your appetite.

535
01:17:14,223 --> 01:17:17,733
You want to say what you want already,
don't you, Zöhre Hatun?

536
01:17:19,037 --> 01:17:23,037
What's done is done, Bahadır.

537
01:17:24,843 --> 01:17:30,073
We struggled a lot, then. It's true.
But now is not the time to fight.

538
01:17:31,196 --> 01:17:36,926
If we understand and trust each other, we'll
surely see the benefit in the future.

539
01:17:38,301 --> 01:17:40,891
What you say is very nice and true.

540
01:17:41,717 --> 01:17:44,617
To be honest, I'm glad you think that way.

541
01:17:45,766 --> 01:17:48,156
It's time for unity, Zöhre Hatun.

542
01:17:49,224 --> 01:17:51,624
My father is in trouble.
He needs support.

543
01:17:52,990 --> 01:17:56,380
I'm sad to hear about Batur.
My condolences.

544
01:17:58,664 --> 01:18:02,664
In a way, I'm your son, too.
And if you are sincere...

545
01:18:03,892 --> 01:18:06,062
I'll be the first one to run to you.

546
01:18:06,742 --> 01:18:10,012
But first, we must help my father.

547
01:18:10,840 --> 01:18:14,840
There is revenge to take,
and scores to settle.

548
01:18:20,130 --> 01:18:23,140
-So, you know what happened?
-I do.

549
01:18:23,454 --> 01:18:24,664
Of course, I do.

550
01:18:24,857 --> 01:18:26,737
I'm already after them.

551
01:18:26,834 --> 01:18:30,404
Saltuk is in prison-tent.
He is no good for my father.

552
01:18:31,764 --> 01:18:35,164
Gündüz Bey is looking for clues.
Hopes for Saltuk's help.

553
01:18:35,389 --> 01:18:39,129
But Saltuk is tough.
I don't think he'll say anything.

554
01:18:41,611 --> 01:18:44,521
Now if you'll allow me.
I want to rest.

555
01:18:44,978 --> 01:18:47,008
Than you, Bahadır.

556
01:18:47,667 --> 01:18:49,097
What can I say...

557
01:18:51,450 --> 01:18:55,450
I didn't know you as a levelheaded man.

558
01:18:55,938 --> 01:18:58,298
Now you are here, welcome.

559
01:18:58,708 --> 01:19:02,708
May Allah clear your path and give you
strenght.

560
01:19:02,899 --> 01:19:04,379
Thank you.

561
01:19:22,795 --> 01:19:26,795
I'm glad my brother Bahadır is here.
He is a support for my father.

562
01:19:26,950 --> 01:19:29,870
A reinforcement to his power.

563
01:19:30,815 --> 01:19:33,235
He is, yes...

564
01:19:34,696 --> 01:19:37,436
There is more to it than just that.

565
01:19:37,598 --> 01:19:40,198
Let's see what will we do when his mother
arrives.

566
01:19:42,559 --> 01:19:44,919
Don't speak like that, mother.

567
01:19:45,054 --> 01:19:47,854
We won't wrangle. We'll stay away and
it will be alright.

568
01:19:49,293 --> 01:19:52,103
Let's get through these hard times.

569
01:19:55,143 --> 01:19:59,143
What good will staying away can do?

570
01:19:59,417 --> 01:20:03,417
Just wait and see what will she do
when she arrives. She is a fox.

571
01:20:04,712 --> 01:20:07,342
No one can deal with her sneakiness.

572
01:20:09,444 --> 01:20:13,444
When she arrives...
We need to look for our back.

573
01:20:15,616 --> 01:20:19,036
Otherwise the snake can strike
at any chance.

574
01:20:26,764 --> 01:20:30,764
Look what Dündar does while you
have so many problems already.

575
01:20:32,878 --> 01:20:36,658
Actually, I should come to the tents with
you and beat him until--

576
01:20:36,675 --> 01:20:37,885
Uncle.

577
01:20:40,907 --> 01:20:43,467
Uncle Dündar has a good heart.

578
01:20:43,505 --> 01:20:46,055
When he finds out the truth...

579
01:20:46,055 --> 01:20:48,685
...he'll know where to stand, for sure.

580
01:20:53,401 --> 01:20:56,191
For years, I've struggled to take over
these names.

581
01:20:56,191 --> 01:20:59,561
I was ripped from my tents, my
loved ones and everything.

582
01:21:01,191 --> 01:21:02,671
And now you have it.

583
01:21:02,737 --> 01:21:04,547
You did it, uncle.

584
01:21:04,832 --> 01:21:08,832
Thanks to you, now we'll
have balance policy with Mongols.

585
01:21:09,670 --> 01:21:12,140
I wouldn't succeed without you.

586
01:21:13,296 --> 01:21:14,786
Thank you.

587
01:21:16,019 --> 01:21:20,019
Council of elders wants to give this
document to the Emperor.

588
01:21:21,040 --> 01:21:25,040
They don't want to deal with Byzantine
while we have the trouble of Mongol.

589
01:21:26,085 --> 01:21:30,085
If the Byzantine Emperor gets rid of
the trouble of Margaret monks...

590
01:21:31,282 --> 01:21:33,282
...we'll be relieved, too.

591
01:21:34,618 --> 01:21:38,238
The trouble of Byzantine stands before
us for centuries, Osman.

592
01:21:38,968 --> 01:21:41,478
They should stand for a little longer,
uncle.

593
01:21:41,643 --> 01:21:44,663
Until we get rid of the Mongols.

594
01:21:47,658 --> 01:21:50,628
When I look into your eyes,
I see your father.

595
01:21:53,421 --> 01:21:55,761
You are valiant just like him.

596
01:21:56,828 --> 01:21:58,648
Clever, just like him.

597
01:22:03,707 --> 01:22:05,237
Thank you.

598
01:22:08,428 --> 01:22:12,428
Who will they have sat on the Byzantine
throne as an Emperor, uncle?

599
01:22:12,941 --> 01:22:15,951
The council of elders waits for the answer
of this question.

600
01:22:16,239 --> 01:22:20,239
There won't be an Emperor but an Empress.

601
01:22:29,994 --> 01:22:31,294
I'm not surprized.

602
01:22:34,055 --> 01:22:34,985
Sofia.

603
01:22:35,203 --> 01:22:36,483
You know her?

604
01:22:36,802 --> 01:22:38,612
I know her heart.

605
01:22:40,001 --> 01:22:41,921
I will rip it soon.

606
01:22:53,663 --> 01:22:56,493
Did you think you can run away from me...

607
01:22:56,614 --> 01:22:58,804
...with that little brain of yours?

608
01:22:59,036 --> 01:23:02,656
Do you think it will end by kidnapping
a poor Bala Hatun, or killing her?

609
01:23:04,391 --> 01:23:08,391
We'll come with our veterans, saints...

610
01:23:08,671 --> 01:23:11,881
...and make these lands a part of
the Islamic world.

611
01:23:15,922 --> 01:23:17,712
Now I think about it...

612
01:23:19,033 --> 01:23:21,423
...you are no good to me alive.

613
01:24:39,492 --> 01:24:41,952
Bala Hatun, you are wounded.

614
01:24:42,024 --> 01:24:43,974
I'm fine, Boran Alp. I'm fine.

615
01:24:44,049 --> 01:24:48,049
Thank you. You arrived in time.

616
01:24:49,189 --> 01:24:50,899
But Helen ran away.

617
01:24:51,863 --> 01:24:53,343
She can't go far.

618
01:24:54,671 --> 01:24:58,671
Alps will take you to the tents.
I'll track her down.

619
01:24:59,588 --> 01:25:02,238
No. Princess Adelfa is under
Osman's protection.

620
01:25:02,304 --> 01:25:03,894
We'll go together.

621
01:25:13,546 --> 01:25:15,606
C'mon, c'mon.

622
01:25:26,648 --> 01:25:31,648
I need to go to Constantinople before it's
too late. Don't tell anyone about me.

623
01:25:31,928 --> 01:25:34,818
Just know that I'll return when my mission
ends.

624
01:25:34,850 --> 01:25:37,090
Don't worry at all, uncle.

625
01:25:37,457 --> 01:25:41,457
Inform me from the Constantinople
where you go as a monk.

626
01:25:43,029 --> 01:25:47,029
I need to know about their intentions,
about the plots they run before us.

627
01:25:47,604 --> 01:25:51,094
I'll need that information. Until we get
rid of Sofya...

628
01:25:51,559 --> 01:25:54,009
...and conquer Kulucahisar.

629
01:25:54,937 --> 01:25:57,857
You never stop, do you?
Just like your father.

630
01:25:57,924 --> 01:26:00,694
In these lands that we take root...

631
01:26:00,694 --> 01:26:03,924
..our branches will go all over the world.

632
01:26:05,514 --> 01:26:08,034
It doesn't fit us to stop.

633
01:26:08,570 --> 01:26:11,870
I won't leave you uninformed, Osman.
Don't worry.

634
01:26:17,928 --> 01:26:19,168
Karayel!

635
01:26:38,645 --> 01:26:42,815
O' passenger! What is your destination?

636
01:26:42,865 --> 01:26:44,985
The holy cause.

637
01:26:47,091 --> 01:26:49,891
May Allah accompany you.

638
01:27:16,454 --> 01:27:20,454
Time is coming. If you'll allow us, we
want to rest a bit.

639
01:27:21,432 --> 01:27:22,322
Sure.

640
01:27:23,862 --> 01:27:26,862
Let's wait for iftar in here.

641
01:27:59,875 --> 01:28:03,875
Yes, Fakir Zülfikar. What do we
have for iftar?

642
01:28:04,495 --> 01:28:07,025
Thank Allah for giving it to us.

643
01:28:07,025 --> 01:28:09,215
We have a bit of honey and some
bread.

644
01:28:09,768 --> 01:28:13,768
Praise Allah who shows us the halal
on the ground...

645
01:28:13,998 --> 01:28:16,458
...and the crescent on the sky.

646
01:28:18,453 --> 01:28:21,063
We've seen another ramadan...

647
01:28:26,818 --> 01:28:29,188
Is this from Kayseri, Zülfikar?

648
01:28:29,452 --> 01:28:33,452
Yes, my Sheikh. One of our
friends, Ahi İlhan sent it.

649
01:28:35,912 --> 01:28:39,912
-May he live long. May Allah bless him.
-Amin.

650
01:28:43,060 --> 01:28:46,200
What a great food that is, isn't it?

651
01:28:47,083 --> 01:28:49,603
For a handful honey, thousands of
bees...

652
01:28:51,381 --> 01:28:54,121
...visit hundreds of thousands of
flowers.

653
01:28:56,066 --> 01:28:58,306
You can't underrate it to ''just bees''.

654
01:28:58,893 --> 01:29:02,103
Qur-an has the sura of Nahl.

655
01:29:03,132 --> 01:29:05,642
Nahl means honey bee.

656
01:29:06,286 --> 01:29:09,566
Honey bees have a sura named after them.

657
01:29:10,225 --> 01:29:14,225
Especially when the tyranny of the
heathens were at peak.

658
01:29:17,028 --> 01:29:19,418
It was such a tyranny...

659
01:29:22,270 --> 01:29:26,270
...many Muslim ate the leaves of trees
to survive.

660
01:29:29,869 --> 01:29:33,869
They ate every piece of leather after...

661
01:29:34,663 --> 01:29:37,553
softening it under fire.

662
01:29:40,116 --> 01:29:44,116
Children and elders starved to death.

663
01:29:47,349 --> 01:29:51,349
The sound of crying mothers and children..

664
01:29:53,145 --> 01:29:56,235
...echoed in the streets of Maqqa.

665
01:30:02,074 --> 01:30:06,364
And then, holy words came.

666
01:30:09,965 --> 01:30:13,965
Friends, there is no time for the lesson
of faith.

667
01:30:14,855 --> 01:30:18,425
It comes on peace time and war time.

668
01:30:19,121 --> 01:30:24,011
Oneness is the first and the lesson in
Islamic school.

669
01:30:28,419 --> 01:30:30,849
''Be like bees'' says Allah.

670
01:30:32,135 --> 01:30:34,015
''Work like bees''

671
01:30:34,594 --> 01:30:37,094
''Stay pure like bees.''

672
01:30:37,236 --> 01:30:41,236
''Produce like bees. And don't
ever stop.''

673
01:30:43,906 --> 01:30:45,906
Muslims didn't stop.

674
01:30:47,471 --> 01:30:51,471
All the pain they carried...

675
01:30:52,084 --> 01:30:56,084
...turned to labour pain, with
the efforts of these Muslims.

676
01:30:58,132 --> 01:31:03,012
A civilized had born from the
womb of Mecca.

677
01:31:08,284 --> 01:31:12,284
Led by our prophet...

678
01:31:14,489 --> 01:31:17,309
...Muslims who worked with the patience
of a bee...

679
01:31:17,740 --> 01:31:21,740
...created things with the taste
of honey.

680
01:31:25,785 --> 01:31:29,785
But polytheists didn't understand the
value of them.

681
01:31:31,691 --> 01:31:37,251
Instead of tasting the honey they made,
they tried to ruin it.

682
01:31:39,792 --> 01:31:42,262
It isn't easy to create.

683
01:31:43,552 --> 01:31:48,942
It takes patience, effort and love.

684
01:31:52,890 --> 01:31:57,420
Of course, there will be ungrateful
people who don't appreciate the honey.

685
01:32:00,941 --> 01:32:06,801
Our cure is hidden in our trouble,
friends.

686
01:32:08,394 --> 01:32:12,784
Just like how the honey is hidden in
flowers.

687
01:33:20,480 --> 01:33:22,270
Save me, my Bey.

688
01:33:23,243 --> 01:33:25,593
-Saltuk?
-They won't show me mercy.

689
01:33:28,697 --> 01:33:31,267
What does it mean, Gündüz Bey?

690
01:33:31,267 --> 01:33:35,537
Since when do you punish an aide
before asking the Bey.

691
01:33:35,813 --> 01:33:39,813
When it's about treason,
being an aide doesn't help, Dündar Bey.

692
01:33:40,394 --> 01:33:43,414
This snake poisoned you, too.
Pity.

693
01:33:44,433 --> 01:33:48,433
This man killed Zorba when he was
about to name the killer of Batur.

694
01:33:52,226 --> 01:33:55,146
What is his aim, uncle?

695
01:33:56,233 --> 01:33:57,313
Speak.

696
01:34:01,080 --> 01:34:02,820
Is it true, Saltuk?

697
01:34:03,247 --> 01:34:05,597
Never, absolutely not, my Bey.

698
01:34:06,010 --> 01:34:08,620
It's a lie.
A slander.

699
01:34:10,749 --> 01:34:14,749
I was hunting. They accuse me because
they've seen me with a bow.

700
01:34:15,146 --> 01:34:17,636
My purpose wasn't killing Zorba.

701
01:34:18,209 --> 01:34:21,299
The arrow on his hand didn't touch Zorba..

702
01:34:25,551 --> 01:34:29,121
..but Zorba was in the reach of the arrow.

703
01:34:33,663 --> 01:34:37,663
Saltuk was caught. It was someone else
who did it.

704
01:34:39,170 --> 01:34:42,240
One who killed Zorba, ran away.

705
01:34:43,184 --> 01:34:46,484
But his secret will be revealed, too.

706
01:34:50,487 --> 01:34:51,607
Now...

707
01:34:52,775 --> 01:34:57,775
...you will tell us all about this.

708
01:34:59,392 --> 01:35:00,352
Uncle.

709
01:35:28,110 --> 01:35:29,950
No sign of her.

710
01:35:30,565 --> 01:35:32,725
We let her go away.

711
01:35:34,382 --> 01:35:37,082
At least, we rescued you from
their hands.

712
01:35:37,858 --> 01:35:41,318
Praise Allah, Bala Hatun.
I don't know what would I tell my Bey.

713
01:35:41,974 --> 01:35:45,974
Thank you, Boran Alp. But we also need
to take the Princess, too.

714
01:35:47,276 --> 01:35:50,106
Otherwise, I'll be embarrassed to
Osman Bey.

715
01:35:50,367 --> 01:35:52,317
He told me to look after her.

716
01:35:58,005 --> 01:36:01,345
Bala Hatun, let's go to the tents.

717
01:36:01,502 --> 01:36:05,722
We know where they are.
We won't leave the princess to them.

718
01:36:16,581 --> 01:36:20,581
Shame on me.
Shame.

719
01:36:22,207 --> 01:36:26,207
My Allah, what will I say to Osman?

720
01:36:39,691 --> 01:36:41,841
These are hard times.

721
01:36:42,654 --> 01:36:46,654
What happened shook
all our balances.

722
01:36:50,160 --> 01:36:52,590
I give his food...

723
01:36:53,157 --> 01:36:55,337
...I keep his leashes...

724
01:36:58,095 --> 01:37:02,095
...when he makes a mistake...

725
01:37:02,135 --> 01:37:04,085
...he is mine to punish.

726
01:37:09,922 --> 01:37:13,342
Saltuk grew up with me.

727
01:37:13,431 --> 01:37:15,331
He can't betray us.

728
01:37:19,489 --> 01:37:23,489
Saltuk! Come here.
Get up.

729
01:37:35,493 --> 01:37:38,543
Mah Allah bless you, my Bey.

730
01:37:38,682 --> 01:37:42,012
Gündüz Bey doesn't have bad
intentions.

731
01:37:44,411 --> 01:37:47,411
He is trying to find the murderer
of his nephew.

732
01:37:47,591 --> 01:37:51,031
Don't you be his enemy.

733
01:37:53,124 --> 01:37:57,124
Follow his orders exactly.

734
01:37:58,657 --> 01:38:00,637
Of course, my Bey.

735
01:38:12,216 --> 01:38:16,216
Very soon, Alişar Bey and my Aygül
will marry.

736
01:38:18,118 --> 01:38:22,118
It's been a long while since Kayı tents
seen entertainment.

737
01:38:22,779 --> 01:38:26,779
I've done my part as an uncle.

738
01:38:27,333 --> 01:38:31,333
I invited you. The rest is up to you.

739
01:38:34,707 --> 01:38:38,707
Aygül is your daughter, and our sister.

740
01:38:39,686 --> 01:38:42,806
Of course, uncle. Of course.

741
01:38:57,196 --> 01:38:58,216
Father.

742
01:39:09,452 --> 01:39:10,262
Don't.

743
01:39:11,327 --> 01:39:12,447
Don't.

744
01:39:18,593 --> 01:39:20,863
Don't even touch my shadow.

745
01:39:21,310 --> 01:39:23,330
Stay away from me!

746
01:39:23,482 --> 01:39:26,422
Father, I came to ask for forgiveness.

747
01:39:47,277 --> 01:39:52,397
You just rest, Bahadır. We'll find a way
to soften my uncle's heart.

748
01:39:53,947 --> 01:39:56,057
Will he forgive me?

749
01:39:57,715 --> 01:40:00,715
What father can resist his son?

750
01:40:04,347 --> 01:40:06,777
You should stay strong.

751
01:40:36,646 --> 01:40:39,596
We couldn't save Adelfa, my Bey.

752
01:40:48,116 --> 01:40:52,066
We checked the grave, my Bey.
The soil is dry.

753
01:40:57,387 --> 01:41:01,247
So, my uncle didn't go to the graveyard.

754
01:41:01,943 --> 01:41:08,703
Son, Dündar is behind this.
We should stop him right now.

755
01:41:10,269 --> 01:41:14,619
If we do it before the wedding, things
will go crazy.

756
01:41:16,588 --> 01:41:22,588
We are in between the devil and the
deep blue sea, Bamsı Bey.

757
01:42:18,014 --> 01:42:21,384
The gazelle couldn't get rid of the
hunters.

758
01:42:21,833 --> 01:42:24,537
With Princess Sofia's regards...

759
01:42:24,537 --> 01:42:27,667
...Princess Adelfa is yours, Alişar Bey.

760
01:42:27,669 --> 01:42:31,099
What about Princess Sofia?
Where is she?

761
01:42:32,299 --> 01:42:35,388
Is she busy with other stuff?

762
01:42:35,388 --> 01:42:40,668
Princess Sofia is working on our alliance,
Alişar Bey.

763
01:42:40,681 --> 01:42:43,191
She will tell you.

764
01:43:01,223 --> 01:43:08,253
When we are done with Kayı Tribe, I will
deliver Princess myself.

765
01:43:10,213 --> 01:43:16,063
Then, in these lands, there will be no
Osman...

766
01:43:16,758 --> 01:43:19,608
...and no Kayı Alps.

767
01:43:22,633 --> 01:43:27,473
Melik.
Take Princess to the dungeon.

768
01:43:28,372 --> 01:43:31,482
Let her rest there.

769
01:44:17,867 --> 01:44:20,996
Your magnificence shakes the tribe
Osman Bey.

770
01:44:20,996 --> 01:44:26,536
Our ancestors say "A horse is ridden by
a Turk."

771
01:44:28,936 --> 01:44:31,406
Welcome, Bahadır.

772
01:44:33,310 --> 01:44:38,010
- What's new?
- I missed it.

773
01:44:38,531 --> 01:44:41,161
I long for here, Osman Bey

774
01:44:42,254 --> 01:44:47,646
I am from Çobanoğulları from my mother's
side, but I belong to here.

775
01:44:47,646 --> 01:44:52,726
Mother side is cool,
but the father side is main.

776
01:44:54,180 --> 01:44:57,918
You are right.
Are you good with my uncle?

777
01:44:57,918 --> 01:45:00,928
No, he is still angry with me.

778
01:45:02,224 --> 01:45:06,534
However, even he couldn't stop me from
coming back here.

779
01:45:06,889 --> 01:45:10,839
If he doesn't take me in, I will pitch a
tent and stay here.

780
01:45:10,852 --> 01:45:13,312
I am not going anywhere.

781
01:45:16,755 --> 01:45:22,178
I heard that he holds you responsible for
Batur's death.

782
01:45:22,178 --> 01:45:26,048
My uncle can't see the truth.

783
01:45:27,983 --> 01:45:34,753
The more humans get elder, the more
they do mistake, Osman Bey.

784
01:45:37,867 --> 01:45:45,087
I said it in the first place, Osman would
love and protect Batur.

785
01:45:45,704 --> 01:45:50,854
But, you know, people talk.

786
01:45:51,288 --> 01:45:54,178
And my father believed.

787
01:45:56,507 --> 01:45:59,747
- Eyvallah (thank you)
- However, I don't think it's you.

788
01:46:00,422 --> 01:46:03,612
I trust you.

789
01:46:03,981 --> 01:46:08,241
Don't think of me as just a person.

790
01:46:08,300 --> 01:46:13,800
Count me as a weapon of yours to
use against the enemy.

791
01:46:15,046 --> 01:46:18,911
I will walk with you.

792
01:46:18,911 --> 01:46:21,981
We will have a lot of time to talk.

793
01:46:22,626 --> 01:46:25,376
Take care of yourself.

794
01:46:45,846 --> 01:46:48,086
Zöhre Hatun.

795
01:46:56,307 --> 01:47:00,047
I know you are worried because Bahadır
is here.

796
01:47:00,567 --> 01:47:04,177
You are right, he was naughty
when he was a kid.

797
01:47:04,354 --> 01:47:12,544
He gave us a hard time with his
rebellious personality. But he changed.

798
01:47:12,837 --> 01:47:16,625
- He changed a lot.
- He will grow up.

799
01:47:16,625 --> 01:47:20,295
He will grow mature.
He will calm down.

800
01:47:21,370 --> 01:47:24,700
However, these are not enough, my Bey.

801
01:47:24,708 --> 01:47:28,647
He betrayed you.
He can...

802
01:47:28,647 --> 01:47:35,627
You say a betrayer can betray again,
huh, Hatun?

803
01:47:36,824 --> 01:47:42,484
If so, I shouldn't have forgiven anyone.

804
01:47:44,423 --> 01:47:50,873
I should have punished everyone who
backdoored me.

805
01:47:52,811 --> 01:47:56,761
Don't bother yourself.

806
01:47:56,830 --> 01:48:04,100
Bahadır's arrival will give us power,
you will see.

807
01:48:10,913 --> 01:48:12,699
We have been summoned, my Bey.

808
01:48:12,699 --> 01:48:16,439
Dowery is in the tent.
Carry it to the carriage.

809
01:48:30,460 --> 01:48:32,858
- My Aygül.
- My Bey father.

810
01:48:32,858 --> 01:48:36,967
We have not smiled for a long time.

811
01:48:36,967 --> 01:48:43,627
Finally, I will be granted with my
daughter's happiness.

812
01:48:44,474 --> 01:48:51,534
Finally, we will be stronger and happier.

813
01:48:52,271 --> 01:48:58,208
First this marriage, then our jobs...

814
01:48:58,208 --> 01:49:02,461
And then, the throne.

815
01:49:02,461 --> 01:49:08,161
We will have what we deserve one by one.

816
01:49:29,953 --> 01:49:32,163
Bala Hatun.

817
01:49:53,302 --> 01:49:55,122
Osman.

818
01:50:05,024 --> 01:50:08,254
Look up, sunshine.

819
01:50:09,243 --> 01:50:12,833
Look up so that I can see your
beautiful face.

820
01:50:13,073 --> 01:50:18,083
I couldn't take care of your entrustment.

821
01:50:18,083 --> 01:50:22,083
How can I look to your face?
Forgive me.

822
01:50:22,293 --> 01:50:29,023
The ones who are to shame are wandering
around, why do you feel embarrassed?

823
01:50:29,254 --> 01:50:36,094
Don't be sad, if there is a betrayer
inside, you can't stop it.

824
01:50:36,257 --> 01:50:44,857
Even if you carried it in your waist,
they would still do what they did.

825
01:50:44,997 --> 01:50:47,107
Don't be sad.

826
01:50:48,170 --> 01:50:52,887
What are we going to do now, Osman?

827
01:50:52,887 --> 01:50:55,537
How can we find the Princess?

828
01:50:55,671 --> 01:50:59,258
Eeh, my Lord sent her to us.

829
01:50:59,258 --> 01:51:04,178
If we are meant to, he will send her
to us again.

830
01:51:04,192 --> 01:51:07,832
Everything happens for a reason, my Bala.

831
01:51:08,509 --> 01:51:11,999
Everything is done by Allah.

832
01:51:13,235 --> 01:51:16,995
What a nice speech of yours,
what a nice look of yours.

833
01:51:17,399 --> 01:51:21,249
You refresh my heart like the water
flooding down to mountains.

834
01:51:21,692 --> 01:51:25,342
May my Lord bless you, inshallah.

835
01:51:25,511 --> 01:51:29,581
May He bless us all, my Bala.

836
01:51:39,330 --> 01:51:41,680
Brother.

837
01:51:42,144 --> 01:51:45,684
- Osman.
- What is up?

838
01:51:55,836 --> 01:51:57,866
Zorba...

839
01:51:58,273 --> 01:52:01,563
They killed him before he talks, right?

840
01:52:07,964 --> 01:52:10,654
Of course, they did.

841
01:52:12,203 --> 01:52:16,664
Betrayers betray.

842
01:52:16,664 --> 01:52:23,164
That's enough, Osman.
We are sick of them.

843
01:52:24,313 --> 01:52:28,503
That's enough, Bamsı Bey.

844
01:52:30,072 --> 01:52:34,842
I tolerated him because he was my uncle,
from my blood.

845
01:52:35,082 --> 01:52:38,032
I didn't try to kill him, but...

846
01:52:38,325 --> 01:52:41,045
We will face them.

847
01:52:43,158 --> 01:52:47,528
We will arrive there and face them.
Let's go!

848
01:52:55,821 --> 01:52:59,066
Dündar Bey, may it be good, inshallah.

849
01:52:59,066 --> 01:53:02,516
Eyvallah, eyvallah (thank you).

850
01:53:13,393 --> 01:53:16,003
Osman is coming, my Bey.

851
01:53:26,112 --> 01:53:31,812
Get in the position.
They may attack.

852
01:53:54,573 --> 01:53:57,803
Where are you going, uncle?

853
01:54:01,651 --> 01:54:05,121
None of your business, Osman.

854
01:54:09,826 --> 01:54:12,417
This game is over.

855
01:54:12,417 --> 01:54:16,197
You can't leave these tents alive.

856
01:54:44,938 --> 01:54:50,418
I am the only one that you haven't
bleed yet, am I not?

857
01:54:50,472 --> 01:54:52,180
Only me.

858
01:54:52,180 --> 01:54:58,470
The games you played now
chained you down. It's time.

859
01:55:00,780 --> 01:55:06,750
How many more lives do you want
to take from these tents, Osman?

860
01:55:08,643 --> 01:55:16,183
Aybars is gone... Bohaç, Erkut, Kantoğlu
have passed away.

861
01:55:17,481 --> 01:55:20,241
They killed my Batur, too.

862
01:55:20,448 --> 01:55:27,398
How much more brave man should die
to satisfy you? Speak, how much?

863
01:55:33,166 --> 01:55:40,576
If you say that ''Uncle, I'll stop after
your blood''...

864
01:55:48,312 --> 01:55:53,677
Come at me, then, my nephew.
Come. Your uncle's blood is halal to you.

865
01:55:53,677 --> 01:55:58,513
Come and hit me with your dark weapon.

866
01:55:58,513 --> 01:56:04,913
So that your rage can end,
your madness can stop.

867
01:56:07,558 --> 01:56:10,548
Father, what are you doing?

868
01:56:10,719 --> 01:56:15,839
Don't meddle. It's between us.

869
01:56:24,700 --> 01:56:31,460
Your blood, your life isn't my trouble,
uncle!

870
01:56:32,074 --> 01:56:36,494
What bothers me is the reputation
of Kayı.

871
01:56:39,059 --> 01:56:44,439
Osman... For the reputation of Kayı...

872
01:56:45,325 --> 01:56:48,615
...I gave up on mine.

873
01:56:49,835 --> 01:56:55,125
I've lost the title of Bey but I still
pledged to Gündüz.

874
01:56:55,225 --> 01:57:01,865
I supported him as long as our tents
stay safe.

875
01:57:05,719 --> 01:57:08,549
Isn't it true, Bamsı Bey?

876
01:57:10,071 --> 01:57:17,063
Speak, Gündüz. Is there any lies in
my words?

877
01:57:17,063 --> 01:57:20,013
Is there? Huh?

878
01:57:20,281 --> 01:57:22,271
Haven't I?

879
01:57:23,817 --> 01:57:29,870
So did I, uncle! I said many times that
Alişar isn't a friend.

880
01:57:29,870 --> 01:57:34,720
What did you do? You took shelter
under him.

881
01:57:35,814 --> 01:57:40,304
Like it wasn't enough, you gave him
Aygül.

882
01:58:04,122 --> 01:58:06,502
Commander Böke.

883
01:58:18,044 --> 01:58:23,024
What's happening, Commander Böke?
Where are your warriors?

884
01:58:24,364 --> 01:58:29,831
Osman... He killed the monks of Margaret.

885
01:58:30,615 --> 01:58:34,400
I said that Osman destroyed everything.
Don't you understand?

886
01:58:34,400 --> 01:58:36,430
How?

887
01:58:37,167 --> 01:58:40,146
How could he know where the Monks of
Margaret are?

888
01:58:40,146 --> 01:58:44,886
Not just that. He knew everything!
Everything!

889
01:58:45,397 --> 01:58:50,612
That I was coming, that why did
we meet. Everything!

890
01:58:50,612 --> 01:58:55,057
Osman! Osman! I'll kill that dog!

891
01:58:55,057 --> 01:59:01,670
You are late, Alişar Bey, late!
Your bannerlord. A tribe bey under you.

892
01:59:01,670 --> 01:59:05,000
You couldn't manage to stop him.

893
01:59:05,644 --> 01:59:09,994
When Geyhatu finds out about it...

894
01:59:11,580 --> 01:59:14,830
...he'll make you pay.

895
01:59:19,647 --> 01:59:24,082
Was I supposed to ask you who should
I give my daughter to, Osman?

896
01:59:24,082 --> 01:59:26,272
Are you a common man, uncle?

897
01:59:26,272 --> 01:59:30,792
How can you give a woman of Kayı...

898
01:59:30,837 --> 01:59:35,454
...to a man who attacks our tents
at any chance...

899
01:59:35,454 --> 01:59:38,874
...and try to sow discontent
among us?

900
01:59:39,799 --> 01:59:43,219
Ahh, Osman.

901
01:59:43,584 --> 01:59:48,174
You don't know how to behave...

902
01:59:48,804 --> 01:59:53,261
If you thought so much of Aygül...

903
01:59:53,261 --> 01:59:58,951
...why did you say no, when I told you
to marry her?

904
02:00:01,648 --> 02:00:08,088
I took you by my side, told you to take
my daughter, so we could be closer...

905
02:00:08,431 --> 02:00:12,571
What did you do? Huh?
What did you do?

906
02:00:18,301 --> 02:00:24,181
Gündüz, do you hear what your
brother says?

907
02:00:25,716 --> 02:00:30,656
You accused in vain.
Failed to prove.

908
02:00:33,533 --> 02:00:38,713
Now you want to hit me by my daughter?

909
02:00:42,498 --> 02:00:46,758
Do you think I gave her by force?

910
02:00:50,309 --> 02:00:56,959
Here, her face is here. Since your
secret is revealed...

911
02:00:57,271 --> 02:00:59,939
...ask to her face...

912
02:00:59,939 --> 02:01:04,439
...does she want this marriage or not?

913
02:01:18,561 --> 02:01:20,491
Uncle!

914
02:01:25,249 --> 02:01:30,259
Are these issues meant to be
spoken in public?

915
02:01:34,710 --> 02:01:36,590
Osman.

916
02:01:38,219 --> 02:01:44,949
We came here to call out.
What did you turn it into?

917
02:01:54,258 --> 02:01:57,088
Keep it short.

918
02:02:03,022 --> 02:02:05,832
I have spoken.

919
02:02:06,450 --> 02:02:12,270
Know that I won't let Aygül marry Alişar.

920
02:02:12,379 --> 02:02:32,639
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries